# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Background {#background}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial demonstrates how to implement the Krylov quantum diagonalization (KQD) algorithm within the context of Qiskit patterns.\n"
"You will first learn the theory behind the algorithm and then see a demonstration of its execution on a QPU.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang tutorial na ito ay nagpapakita kung paano ipatupad ang Krylov quantum diagonalization (KQD) algorithm sa konteksto ng Qiskit patterns.\n"
"Matututunan mo muna ang teorya sa likod ng algorithm at pagkatapos ay makikita mo ang demonstrasyon ng pagpapatupad nito sa QPU.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Estimating the low-energy properties of many-body Hamiltonians is a central task in quantum simulation.\n"
"For example, ground-state energies and low-lying excitations are directly related to chemical stability, magnetic ordering, quantum phase transitions, and material response.\n"
"On a classical computer, the Hilbert-space dimension grows exponentially with the number of orbitals or spins, so direct diagonalization quickly becomes impractical.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagtantiya sa mga low-energy property ng many-body Hamiltonians ay isang pangunahing gawain sa quantum simulation.\n"
"Halimbawa, ang mga ground-state energy at low-lying excitation ay direktang kaugnay sa chemical stability, magnetic ordering, quantum phase transitions, at material response.\n"
"Sa isang classical computer, lumalaki nang exponential ang Hilbert-space dimension kasabay ng bilang ng orbitals o spins, kaya't mabilis na nagiging hindi praktikal ang direktang diagonalization.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are several quantum-computing approaches to this problem.\n"
"Near-term variational methods, such as the [variational quantum eigensolver (VQE)](/tutorials/spin-chain-vqe), use relatively shallow parameterized circuits, but they require a nonlinear classical optimization loop with many quantum-circuit evaluations.\n"
"At the other end, [quantum phase estimation (QPE)](https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0604193) provides a more direct route to eigenvalue estimation with rigorous guarantees, but standard QPE requires long coherent circuits and is mainly suited to fault-tolerant quantum computers.\n"
"KQD sits between these two approaches: it uses real-time Hamiltonian evolution, as in phase-estimation-based algorithms, but replaces full phase estimation with a compact projected eigenvalue problem that can be solved classically.\n"
msgstr ""
"May ilang quantum-computing na paraan para sa problemang ito.\n"
"Ginagamit ng mga near-term variational method, tulad ng [variational quantum eigensolver (VQE)](/tutorials/spin-chain-vqe), ang medyo shallow na parameterized circuits, ngunit kailangan nila ng isang nonlinear classical optimization loop na may maraming quantum-circuit evaluation.\n"
"Sa kabilang banda, nagbibigay ang [quantum phase estimation (QPE)](https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0604193) ng mas direktang daan patungo sa eigenvalue estimation na may mahigpit na garantiya, ngunit nangangailangan ang standard QPE ng mahahabang coherent circuits at pangunahing angkop para sa fault-tolerant na quantum computers.\n"
"Nasa gitna ng dalawang paraang ito ang KQD: ginagamit nito ang real-time Hamiltonian evolution, tulad ng sa mga phase-estimation-based na algorithm, ngunit pinapalitan ang full phase estimation ng isang compact projected eigenvalue problem na malulutas nang classical.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider an $n$-qubit Hamiltonian $H$ and a reference state $\\lvert \\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
"The KQD method builds a Krylov subspace from real-time evolved states,\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang ang isang $n$-qubit Hamiltonian $H$ at isang reference state $\\lvert \\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
"Bumubuo ang KQD method ng isang Krylov subspace mula sa real-time evolved states,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle = e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t H}\\lvert \\psi_{0}\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\ell = 0,1,\\ldots,r-1,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle = e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t H}\\lvert \\psi_{0}\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\ell = 0,1,\\ldots,r-1,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $r$ is the Krylov dimension and $\\Delta t$ is the time step.\n"
"Any state in the Krylov subspace is then represented as a linear combination of these basis states,\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $r$ ay ang Krylov dimension at ang $\\Delta t$ ay ang time step.\n"
"Anumang state sa Krylov subspace ay ipinapakita bilang isang linear combination ng mga basis states na ito,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi(\\mathbf{c})\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi(\\mathbf{c})\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell \\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle}\n"
"{\\left\\|\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell \\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle\\right\\|},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where the denominator normalizes the state.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell \\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle}\n"
"{\\left\\|\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell \\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle\\right\\|},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where the denominator normalizes the state.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With simple algebra, we can see that the corresponding energy is written as the Rayleigh quotient,\n"
msgstr "Sa simpleng algebra, makikita natin na ang katumbas na energy ay isinusulat bilang Rayleigh quotient,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"E(\\mathbf{c})\n"
"=\\langle \\psi(\\mathbf{c})|H|\\psi(\\mathbf{c}) \\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{\n"
"\\sum_{k,\\ell} c_k^* c_\\ell \\langle \\psi_k\\vert H\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"}{\n"
"\\sum_{k,\\ell} c_k^* c_\\ell \\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"E(\\mathbf{c})\n"
"=\\langle \\psi(\\mathbf{c})|H|\\psi(\\mathbf{c}) \\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{\n"
"\\sum_{k,\\ell} c_k^* c_\\ell \\langle \\psi_k\\vert H\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"}{\n"
"\\sum_{k,\\ell} c_k^* c_\\ell \\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{\n"
"\\mathbf{c}^{\\dagger}\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}\n"
"}{\n"
"\\mathbf{c}^{\\dagger}\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}\n"
"}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{\n"
"\\mathbf{c}^{\\dagger}\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}\n"
"}{\n"
"\\mathbf{c}^{\\dagger}\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}\n"
"}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, the matrices $\\mathcal{S}$ and $\\mathcal{H}$,\n"
msgstr "Dito, ang mga matrices $\\mathcal{S}$ at $\\mathcal{H}$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}=\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}=\\langle \\psi_k\\vert H\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}=\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}=\\langle \\psi_k\\vert H\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"define the projected overlap and Hamiltonian matrices.\n"
"Their entries are estimated using quantum-circuit measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"ay tumutukoy sa projected overlap at Hamiltonian matrices.\n"
"Ang kanilang mga entry ay tinatantiya gamit ang quantum-circuit measurements.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We aim to find the coefficient $\\mathbf{c}$ that gives the minimum $E(\\mathbf{c})$:\n"
msgstr "Layunin nating hanapin ang coefficient $\\mathbf{c}$ na nagbibigay ng minimum $E(\\mathbf{c})$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\min_{\\mathbf{c}\\neq \\mathbf{0}} E(\\mathbf{c}).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\min_{\\mathbf{c}\\neq \\mathbf{0}} E(\\mathbf{c}).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By the Rayleigh-Ritz theorem, this minimization is equivalent to solving the generalized eigenvalue problem (GEVP),\n"
msgstr "Ayon sa Rayleigh-Ritz theorem, katumbas ng minimization na ito ang paglutas ng generalized eigenvalue problem (GEVP),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}=E \\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}=E \\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the dimension $r$ can be small enough for a classical computer to solve the GEVP.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na ang dimension $r$ ay maaaring maliit nang sapat para lutasin ng isang classical computer ang GEVP.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the same variational principle used in classical subspace diagonalization, but here the basis states are generated by quantum time evolution.\n"
"Compared with VQE, KQD usually requires deeper circuits because it relies on real-time evolution.\n"
"In return, KQD avoids nonlinear parameter optimization and iterative quantum-hardware execution, and it systematically improves as the projected subspace is enlarged.\n"
"The algorithm has been demonstrated at large scale on existing quantum hardware [\\[2\\]](#references), and its performance can be analyzed with provable guarantees [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ang parehong variational principle na ginagamit sa classical subspace diagonalization, ngunit dito, nabubuo ang mga basis state sa pamamagitan ng quantum time evolution.\n"
"Kung ikukumpara sa VQE, karaniwang nangangailangan ang KQD ng mas malalim na circuits dahil umaasa ito sa real-time evolution.\n"
"Bilang kapalit, iniiwasan ng KQD ang nonlinear parameter optimization at iterative quantum-hardware execution, at systematic itong bumubuti habang pinapalawak ang projected subspace.\n"
"Naipakita na ang algorithm sa malaking sukat sa umiiral na quantum hardware [\\[2\\]](#references), at maaaring suriin ang performance nito na may mapapatunayang garantiya [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"

