# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian and reference state {#hamiltonian-and-reference-state}"
msgstr "Hamiltonian and reference state {#hamiltonian-and-reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example uses a 12-qubit open-boundary Heisenberg chain ($n=12$),\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng halimbawang ito ang isang 12-qubit open-boundary Heisenberg chain ($n=12$),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\left(X_iX_{i+1}+Y_iY_{i+1}+Z_iZ_{i+1}\\right),\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\left(X_iX_{i+1}+Y_iY_{i+1}+Z_iZ_{i+1}\\right),\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with a single-excitation product state\n"
msgstr "na may single-excitation product state\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=|000001000000\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=|000001000000\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"as the reference state.\n"
"Because the Heisenberg Hamiltonian defined above conserves the total number of excitations, the reference state stays in the single-excitation subspace, whose dimension grows only linearly with the number of qubits. We can therefore compute the exact ground-state energy efficiently, by diagonalizing the Hamiltonian restricted to that subspace, and use it purely as a diagnostic benchmark for the KQD estimate. The KQD workflow itself estimates projected matrix elements by using Qiskit primitives and solves the resulting projected problem classically.\n"
msgstr ""
"bilang reference state.\n"
"Dahil ang Heisenberg Hamiltonian na ipinakita sa itaas ay nagpapanatili ng kabuuang bilang ng excitations, nananatili ang reference state sa single-excitation subspace, na ang dimension ay lumalaki lamang nang linear kasabay ng bilang ng qubits. Kaya naman, magagawa nating i-compute nang epektibo ang eksaktong ground-state energy, sa pamamagitan ng pag-diagonalize ng Hamiltonian na nilimitahan sa subspace na iyon, at gamitin ito bilang isang diagnostic benchmark lamang para sa KQD estimate. Tinatantiya mismo ng KQD workflow ang mga projected matrix element gamit ang Qiskit primitives at lulutasin nang classical ang resultang projected problem.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the parameters for the algorithm {#set-the-parameters-for-the-algorithm}"
msgstr "Itakda ang mga parameter para sa algorithm {#set-the-parameters-for-the-algorithm}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Based on the upper-bounds on the Hamiltonian norm, Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references) heuristically suggests the time step $\\Delta t$ as $\\pi/\\|H\\|$.\n"
"Because the spectral norm $\\|H\\|$ is hard to compute, we instead use its upper bound:\n"
msgstr ""
"Batay sa mga upper-bound sa Hamiltonian norm, iminumungkahi nang heuristic ng Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references) ang time step $\\Delta t$ bilang $\\pi/\\|H\\|$.\n"
"Dahil mahirap i-compute ang spectral norm $\\|H\\|$, ginagamit natin sa halip ang upper bound nito:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\|H\\| \\le \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\underbrace{\\|X_i X_{i+1}+Y_{i} Y_{i+1}+Z_{i} Z_{i+1}\\|}_{4 \\times 4 \\text{ matrix, easy to calculate the norm}} = 3(n-1).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\|H\\| \\le \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\underbrace{\\|X_i X_{i+1}+Y_{i} Y_{i+1}+Z_{i} Z_{i+1}\\|}_{4 \\times 4 \\text{ matrix, easy to calculate the norm}} = 3(n-1).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We set the Krylov dimension to $r=10$ and the number of Trotter steps per time step to $5$: a large enough Krylov space to resolve the low-lying spectrum while keeping the deepest circuit ($t_{\\max}=(r-1)\\Delta t$) affordable, and enough Trotter steps to keep the discretization error small at that deepest circuit.\n"
msgstr "Itinatakda natin ang Krylov dimension sa $r=10$ at ang bilang ng Trotter steps kada time step sa $5$: isang Krylov space na malaki nang sapat upang malutas ang low-lying spectrum habang pinapanatiling abot-kaya ang pinakamalalim na circuit ($t_{\\max}=(r-1)\\Delta t$), at sapat na bilang ng Trotter steps upang panatilihing maliit ang discretization error sa pinakamalalim na circuit na iyon.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build circuit {#build-circuit}"
msgstr "Build circuit {#build-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we build the circuits to estimate the matrix elements $\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}$ and $\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}$.\n"
"Because all powers of $H$ commute, we have\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito, bubuo tayo ng mga circuit upang tantiyahin ang mga matrix element na $\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}$ at $\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}$.\n"
"Dahil nag-commute ang lahat ng powers ng $H$, mayroon tayong\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|H e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{H}_{0,\\ell-k},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|H e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{H}_{0,\\ell-k},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{S}_{0,\\ell-k}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"Such matrices where the elements depend on the index differences in this manner are called *Toeplitz* and can be reconstructed from first-row elements indexed by $d=\\ell-k$.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{S}_{0,\\ell-k}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"Such matrices where the elements depend on the index differences in this manner are called *Toeplitz* and can be reconstructed from first-row elements indexed by $d=\\ell-k$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we present the circuit, called **extended-swap-test**, which prepares\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $|\\psi_d\\rangle=e^{-id\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito, ipinapakita natin ang circuit, tinatawag na **extended-swap-test**, na naghahanda ng\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"kung saan ang $|\\psi_d\\rangle=e^{-id\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reference state {#reference-state}"
msgstr "Reference state {#reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We prepare the reference state $|\\psi_0\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Inihahanda natin ang reference state $|\\psi_0\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/fb2879c5-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/fb2879c5-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time evolution {#time-evolution}"
msgstr "Time evolution {#time-evolution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Realize the time-evolution operator generated by the Hamiltonian, approximated by simple [Lie-Trotterization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter).\n"
msgstr "Isakatuparan ang time-evolution operator na nabuo ng Hamiltonian, na tinatantiya sa pamamagitan ng simpleng [Lie-Trotterization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter).\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/017b8548-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/017b8548-0.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extended swap test circuit [\\[3\\]](#references) {#extended-swap-test-circuit-3references}"
msgstr "Extended swap test circuit [\\[3\\]](#references) {#extended-swap-test-circuit-3references}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit first prepares the reference state on the system register while the ancilla remains in $|0\\rangle$:\n"
msgstr "Inihahanda muna ng circuit ang reference state sa system register habang nananatili ang ancilla sa $|0\\rangle$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_{0}\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_{0}\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then, applying a Hadamard gate to the ancilla creates a coherent superposition of two branches:\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos, ang paglalagay ng Hadamard gate sa ancilla ay lumilikha ng isang coherent superposition ng dalawang branch:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, the controlled time-evolution gate applies:\n"
msgstr "Sa huli, inilalapat ang controlled time-evolution gate:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t=d\\Delta t) = e^{-id\\Delta t H}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t=d\\Delta t) = e^{-id\\Delta t H}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "only when the ancilla is in the $|1\\rangle$ branch. Therefore,\n"
msgstr "tanging lamang kapag nasa $|1\\rangle$ branch ang ancilla. Samakatuwid,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the next code block, we implement:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Psi(t)\\rangle = \\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"which will be assigned as $t=d\\Delta t$ for $d=1,\\cdots r-1$ in the execution step.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa susunod na code block, ipinapatupad natin ang:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Psi(t)\\rangle = \\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"na itatalaga bilang $t=d\\Delta t$ para sa $d=1,\\cdots r-1$ sa execution step.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/1260f66a-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/1260f66a-0.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Observables {#observables}"
msgstr "Observables {#observables}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For any Hermitian system observable $O$, here we set the observables to calculate:\n"
msgstr "Para sa anumang Hermitian system observable $O$, itinatakda natin dito ang mga observable na kakalkulahin:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"z=\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"z=\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is because $O=I$ gives the overlap element $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle$, while $O=H$ gives the Hamiltonian element $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Dahil ito ay dahil ang $O=I$ ay nagbibigay ng overlap element $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle$, habang ang $O=H$ ay nagbibigay ng Hamiltonian element $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using $X=|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$, we have\n"
msgstr "Gamit ang $X=|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$, mayroon tayong\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|X\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(X\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{z+z^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|X\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(X\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{z+z^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Re} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Re} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Similarly, using $Y=-i|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$,\n"
msgstr "Katulad nito, gamit ang $Y=-i|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(Y\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"-i\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"i\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{-iz+iz^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(Y\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"-i\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"i\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{-iz+iz^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Im} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Im} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, we have\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|X\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Samakatuwid, mayroon tayong\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|X\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Re}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Re}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Im}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Im}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, for each state $|\\Psi_{0d}\\rangle$, we need to measure:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"X \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"X \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{H}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{H}_{0d}.\\\\\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa huli, para sa bawat state $|\\Psi_{0d}\\rangle$, kailangan nating sukatin:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"X \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"X \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{H}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{H}_{0d}.\\\\\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the estimation of the $\\mathcal{H}$ matrix elements, the number of Pauli terms is much larger than that for the $\\mathcal{S}$ matrix elements.\n"
msgstr "Para sa pagtantiya ng mga matrix element ng $\\mathcal{H}$, mas malaki nang husto ang bilang ng Pauli terms kaysa sa mga matrix element ng $\\mathcal{S}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now reduce the number of measured Hamiltonian terms by using a shifting technique [\\[4\\]](#references).\n"
"We split the Hamiltonian as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari na nating bawasan ang bilang ng mga sinusukat na Hamiltonian terms gamit ang isang shifting technique [\\[4\\]](#references).\n"
"Hinahati natin ang Hamiltonian bilang:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H = (H-T) + T,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H = (H-T) + T,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $T$ is chosen such that the reference state is its eigenstate,\n"
msgstr "kung saan pinili ang $T$ upang ang reference state ay maging eigenstate nito,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then,\n"
msgstr "Then,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{0d}\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|T|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{0d}\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|T|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here,\n"
msgstr "Here,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is the shifted Hamiltonian matrix element.\n"
"Therefore, we only need to measure $X\\otimes (H-T)$ and $Y\\otimes (H-T)$.\n"
"The contribution from $T$ is reconstructed classically using the already measured overlap matrix element $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"ay ang shifted Hamiltonian matrix element.\n"
"Samakatuwid, kailangan lang nating sukatin ang $X\\otimes (H-T)$ at $Y\\otimes (H-T)$.\n"
"Ang kontribusyon mula sa $T$ ay muling ibinubuo nang classical gamit ang nasukat na nang overlap matrix element na $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this example, a natural choice is the diagonal part of the Heisenberg Hamiltonian,\n"
msgstr "Sa halimbawang ito, natural na pagpipilian ang diagonal na bahagi ng Heisenberg Hamiltonian,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the reference state is a computational-basis state, it is an eigenstate of every $Z_iZ_{i+1}$ term.\n"
msgstr "Dahil ang reference state ay isang computational-basis state, ito ay isang eigenstate ng bawat $Z_iZ_{i+1}$ term.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, a more advantageous choice is to include not only the diagonal $ZZ$ terms, but also the $XX+YY$ terms that annihilate the reference state.\n"
msgstr "Gayunpaman, mas mainam na pagpipilian ang isama hindi lamang ang diagonal na mga $ZZ$ terms, kundi pati na rin ang mga $XX+YY$ terms na nag-a-annihilate sa reference state.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each neighboring pair, the operator $XX+YY$ satisfies\n"
msgstr "Para sa bawat katabing pares, natutugunan ng operator na $XX+YY$ ang\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|00\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|11\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|00\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|11\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and\n"
msgstr "and\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|01\\rangle = 2|10\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|10\\rangle = 2|01\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|01\\rangle = 2|10\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|10\\rangle = 2|01\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, the $XX+YY$ term contributes only when the two neighboring qubits have different occupations in the reference bitstring.\n"
"If the two qubits are both $0$ or both $1$, the term annihilates the reference state and can also be shifted out.\n"
msgstr ""
"Samakatuwid, nagbibigay ng kontribusyon ang $XX+YY$ term lamang kapag magkaiba ang occupation ng dalawang katabing qubit sa reference bitstring.\n"
"Kung parehong $0$ o parehong $1$ ang dalawang qubit, na-a-annihilate ng term ang reference state at maaari ring alisin sa pamamagitan ng shifting.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let $|\\psi_{\\rm ref}\\rangle = |z_0\\cdots z_{n-1}\\rangle$, where $z_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$.\n"
"Thus, we can choose\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{z_i={z_{i+1}}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Hayaang $|\\psi_{\\rm ref}\\rangle = |z_0\\cdots z_{n-1}\\rangle$, kung saan ang $z_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$.\n"
"Sa gayon, maaari nating piliin ang\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{z_i={z_{i+1}}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This operator still satisfies\n"
msgstr "Natutugunan pa rin ng operator na ito ang\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"because the $ZZ$ terms act diagonally on $|\\psi_0\\rangle$, while the shifted $XX+YY$ terms give zero.\n"
"The corresponding eigenvalue is therefore determined only by the $ZZ$ terms,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\tau = \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\n"
"(-1)^{z_i}\n"
"(-1)^{z_{i+1}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"dahil ang mga $ZZ$ terms ay kumikilos nang diagonal sa $|\\psi_0\\rangle$, habang nagbibigay ng zero ang mga shifted $XX+YY$ terms.\n"
"Ang katumbas na eigenvalue ay natutukoy lamang, kung gayon, ng mga $ZZ$ terms,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\tau = \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\n"
"(-1)^{z_i}\n"
"(-1)^{z_{i+1}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this choice, the shifted Hamiltonian becomes:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H-T = \\sum_{z_i\\ne z_{i+1}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pagpiling ito, ang shifted Hamiltonian ay nagiging:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H-T = \\sum_{z_i\\ne z_{i+1}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a result, only the edges with different occupations in the reference state need to be measured.\n"
"All $ZZ$ terms and all inactive $XX+YY$ terms are reconstructed through the overlap contribution $\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}$, or give zero contribution by construction.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilang resulta, kailangan lamang sukatin ang mga edge na may magkaibang occupation sa reference state.\n"
"Lahat ng $ZZ$ terms at lahat ng inactive na $XX+YY$ terms ay muling ibinubuo sa pamamagitan ng overlap contribution na $\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}$, o nagbibigay ng zero na kontribusyon dahil sa disenyo nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This gives a smaller observable than shifting only the diagonal part.\n"
"In particular, for a computational-basis reference state with a localized excitation, only the edges adjacent to the excitation remain in $H-T$.\n"
"Therefore, the number of Pauli terms in $X\\otimes(H-T)$ and $Y\\otimes(H-T)$ can be substantially reduced, while the reconstructed matrix element\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagbibigay ito ng mas maliit na observable kaysa sa pag-shift lamang ng diagonal na bahagi.\n"
"Partikular na, para sa isang computational-basis reference state na may localized excitation, ang mga edge lamang na katabi ng excitation ang nananatili sa $H-T$.\n"
"Kaya naman, ang bilang ng mga Pauli terms sa $X\\otimes(H-T)$ at $Y\\otimes(H-T)$ ay maaaring bawasan nang malaki, habang ang muling ibinubuong matrix element\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "remains exactly the same.\n"
msgstr "ay nananatiling eksaktong pareho.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we turn the abstract extended-swap-test circuit into a hardware-oriented template.\n"
"Before that, we further optimize the circuit in the abstract level first.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ay ginagawa nating hardware-oriented template ang abstract na extended-swap-test circuit.\n"
"Bago iyon, pinapabuti pa natin ang circuit sa abstract level muna.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare Hamiltonian term ordering {#compare-hamiltonian-term-ordering}"
msgstr "Compare Hamiltonian term ordering {#compare-hamiltonian-term-ordering}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we compare different orderings of the Pauli terms in the Heisenberg Hamiltonian for the Hamiltonian simulation.\n"
"The Hamiltonian itself is unchanged, but the ordering affects how the product-formula circuit is generated and how much the structure can be parallelized in the circuit.\n"
"For example, the naive ordering lists all nearest-neighbor $XX$ terms, then all $YY$ terms, then all $ZZ$ terms.\n"
"This places adjacent edges such as $(0,1)$ and $(1,2)$ next to each other, so they cannot be executed in parallel.\n"
"The even-then-odd ordering visits disjoint even edges first, followed by odd edges, which exposes parallel two-qubit layers.\n"
"The even-odd edge-grouped ordering goes one step further: for each edge, it keeps the local $XX$, $YY$, and $ZZ$ terms together, while still visiting even edges before odd edges.\n"
"We expect the even-then-odd and even-odd edge-grouped orderings to reduce circuit depth by exposing parallel two-qubit layers, and the edge-grouped ordering to additionally reduce the Trotter error because the local two-qubit interaction on the same edge is handled as a compact block.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, ihahambing natin ang iba't ibang ordering ng mga Pauli terms sa Heisenberg Hamiltonian para sa Hamiltonian simulation.\n"
"Hindi nagbabago ang mismong Hamiltonian, ngunit apektado ng ordering kung paano nabubuo ang product-formula circuit at kung gaano ka-parallel ang istruktura sa circuit.\n"
"Halimbawa, inilalayo ng naive na ordering ang lahat ng nearest-neighbor $XX$ terms, pagkatapos lahat ng $YY$ terms, at pagkatapos lahat ng $ZZ$ terms.\n"
"Inilalagay nito ang mga katabing edge tulad ng $(0,1)$ at $(1,2)$ sa tabi ng isa't isa, kaya't hindi sila maaaring i-execute nang parallel.\n"
"Binibisita muna ng even-then-odd na ordering ang disjoint na mga even edge, sinusundan ng odd edges, na naglalantad ng parallel two-qubit layers.\n"
"Lampas pa rito ang even-odd edge-grouped na ordering: para sa bawat edge, pinananatili nitong magkasama ang local na $XX$, $YY$, at $ZZ$ terms, habang binibisita pa rin ang even edges bago ang odd edges.\n"
"Inaasahan nating babawasan ng even-then-odd at even-odd edge-grouped orderings ang circuit depth sa pamamagitan ng paglalantad ng parallel two-qubit layers, at babawasan pa ng edge-grouped ordering ang Trotter error dahil ang local two-qubit interaction sa parehong edge ay hinahawakan bilang compact block.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Pauli evolutions with different term ordering](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/ham_ordering.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Pauli evolutions with different term ordering](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/ham_ordering.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Hamiltonian ordering also affects the Trotter error.\n"
"If we place noncommuting terms next to each other, the basis transitions occur more often, which induces more Trotter error.\n"
"By grouping terms that require the same Pauli-basis transformation, redundant basis-changes can be avoided.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apektado rin ng Hamiltonian ordering ang Trotter error.\n"
"Kung inilalagay natin ang mga noncommuting terms sa tabi ng isa't isa, mas madalas magaganap ang basis transitions, na nagdudulot ng mas maraming Trotter error.\n"
"Sa pamamagitan ng pagpapangkat ng mga terms na nangangailangan ng parehong Pauli-basis transformation, maiiwasan ang mga redundant na basis-changes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, the comparison uses the largest evolution time that appears in the first-row Krylov estimates,\n"
"$t_{\\max} = (r-1)\\Delta t,$\n"
"using the same transpilation condition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito, ginagamit ng paghahambing ang pinakamalaking evolution time na lumilitaw sa first-row Krylov estimates,\n"
"$t_{\\max} = (r-1)\\Delta t,$\n"
"gamit ang parehong transpilation condition.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In order to measure the Trotter error, we use **process infidelity** between the Trotterized circuit and the exact Hamiltonian evolution,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\text{Infidelity}(U,V)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang sukatin ang Trotter error, ginagamit natin ang **process infidelity** sa pagitan ng Trotterized circuit at ng eksaktong Hamiltonian evolution,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\text{Infidelity}(U,V)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1-F(U,V)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"1-F(U,V)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1 - \\frac{|\\operatorname{Tr}(U^\\dagger V)|^2}{d^2},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d=2^n$ is the dimension of the Hilbert space.\n"
msgstr ""
"1 - \\frac{|\\operatorname{Tr}(U^\\dagger V)|^2}{d^2},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d=2^n$ is the dimension of the Hilbert space.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This diagnostic uses dense matrices, so it is suitable for this small 12-qubit example but not intended as a scalable subroutine.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang diagnostic na ito ng dense matrices, kaya't angkop ito para sa maliit na 12-qubit na halimbawang ito ngunit hindi ito nilalayong maging scalable na subroutine.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We first keep the synthesis rule fixed to one first-order Trotter step and vary only the Pauli-term ordering.\n"
"The goal of this comparison is mainly to see how much circuit depth and two-qubit cost can be reduced by exposing disjoint nearest-neighbor edges to the transpiler.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pinananatili muna nating fixed ang synthesis rule sa isang first-order Trotter step at pinapabago lamang ang Pauli-term ordering.\n"
"Ang layunin ng paghahambing na ito ay pangunahing makita kung gaano kalaki ang mababawasan sa circuit depth at two-qubit cost sa pamamagitan ng paglalantad ng disjoint na nearest-neighbor edges sa transpiler.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-1.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-3.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-5.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-5.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At `reps=1`, we observe that even-then-odd and even-odd edge-grouped orderings both collapse the depth from 15 to 6 by exposing parallel two-qubit layers, while the two-qubit gate count stays the same across all three orderings.\n"
"However, all three orderings have infidelity close to 1, so we sweep the number of Trotter repetitions to separate the orderings more clearly.\n"
"As the number of repetitions grows, the infidelity of `even-odd edge-grouped` ordering drops faster than the other two, reaching 0.045 at `reps=8` versus 0.075 for naive and even-then-odd ordering.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa `reps=1`, napapansin natin na parehong pinapababa ng even-then-odd at even-odd edge-grouped orderings ang depth mula 15 patungong 6 sa pamamagitan ng paglalantad ng parallel two-qubit layers, habang nananatiling pareho ang two-qubit gate count sa lahat ng tatlong ordering.\n"
"Gayunpaman, malapit sa 1 ang infidelity ng lahat ng tatlong ordering, kaya't sinusuri natin ang bilang ng Trotter repetitions upang mas malinaw na ihiwalay ang mga ordering.\n"
"Habang lumalaki ang bilang ng repetitions, mas mabilis bumaba ang infidelity ng `even-odd edge-grouped` na ordering kaysa sa dalawang iba pa, umaabot sa 0.045 sa `reps=8` kumpara sa 0.075 para sa naive at even-then-odd na ordering.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare product-formula synthesis {#compare-product-formula-synthesis}"
msgstr "Compare product-formula synthesis {#compare-product-formula-synthesis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we explore different advanced settings of Trotterization, with the fixed Hamiltonian ordering to the even-odd edge-grouped ordering.\n"
"We consider first-order Lie-Trotter, second-order Suzuki-Trotter, and fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, sinusuri natin ang iba't ibang advanced na setting ng Trotterization, na may fixed na Hamiltonian ordering sa even-odd edge-grouped ordering.\n"
"Isinasaalang-alang natin ang first-order Lie-Trotter, second-order Suzuki-Trotter, at fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Lie-Trotter gives the shallowest circuit but has the largest error, while the fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter is more accurate but increases the circuit depth.\n"
"For the rest of the tutorial, we choose second-order Suzuki-Trotter because it gives a small-depth circuit while substantially reducing the Trotter error relative to the first-order formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagbibigay ang Lie-Trotter ng pinakamababaw na circuit ngunit may pinakamalaking error, habang mas tumpak ang fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter ngunit nagpapataas ito ng circuit depth.\n"
"Para sa natitirang bahagi ng tutorial, pinipili natin ang second-order Suzuki-Trotter dahil nagbibigay ito ng maliit na depth na circuit habang malaking-lakas na binabawasan ang Trotter error kumpara sa first-order formula.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remove the controlled time-evolution gate {#remove-the-controlled-time-evolution-gate}"
msgstr "Remove the controlled time-evolution gate {#remove-the-controlled-time-evolution-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the extended swap test, controlling time evolution with a single ancilla qubit requires the ancilla to control many gates across the system.\n"
"This can introduce substantial routing overhead and, in the worst case, effectively requires all-to-one connectivity.\n"
"To avoid this, further optimization is possible by replacing the controlled time-evolution gate with a control-free version, exploiting the symmetry of the Hamiltonian.\n"
"Let's observe the following circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa extended swap test, ang pagkontrol sa time evolution gamit ang iisang ancilla qubit ay nangangailangan ng ancilla na kumontrol sa maraming gates sa buong system.\n"
"Maaari itong magdulot ng malaking routing overhead at, sa pinakamasamang kaso, epektibong nangangailangan ng all-to-one connectivity.\n"
"Upang maiwasan ito, posible ang karagdagang optimization sa pamamagitan ng pagpapalit ng controlled time-evolution gate ng control-free na bersyon, na sinasamantala ang symmetry ng Hamiltonian.\n"
"Masdan natin ang sumusunod na circuit.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![circuit optimization](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/circuit_opt.avif)\n"
msgstr "![circuit optimization](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/circuit_opt.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, $B_{\\rm ref}$ prepares the reference state, $B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle = |\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Dito, inihahanda ng $B_{\\rm ref}$ ang reference state, $B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle = |\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of first preparing $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)|\\psi_0\\rangle$ and then applying $U(t)$ only on the $|1\\rangle$ branch, the circuit directly prepares the two branches as\n"
msgstr "Sa halip na unang ihanda ang $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)|\\psi_0\\rangle$ at pagkatapos ilapat ang $U(t)$ sa $|1\\rangle$ branch lamang, direktang inihahanda ng circuit ang dalawang branch bilang\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where\n"
msgstr "where\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle = U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle = U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit first applies a Hadamard gate to the ancilla and prepares the reference state only on the $|1\\rangle$ branch:\n"
msgstr "Unang inilalapat ng circuit ang Hadamard gate sa ancilla at inihahanda ang reference state sa $|1\\rangle$ branch lamang:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then the uncontrolled time-evolution operator is applied to both branches:\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos, inilalapat ang uncontrolled time-evolution operator sa parehong branch:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since the Hamiltonian preserves the excitation number, we can see that $|0^n\\rangle$ is its eigenstate, and thus\n"
"the evolution operator only accumulates a phase under the Hamiltonian:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t)|0^n\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil pinapanatili ng Hamiltonian ang excitation number, makikita natin na ang $|0^n\\rangle$ ay eigenstate nito, at kaya lamang naipupundo ng evolution operator ay isang phase sa ilalim ng Hamiltonian:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t)|0^n\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0^n\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0^n\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore,\n"
msgstr "Therefore,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, $B_{\\rm ref}$ is applied only on the $|0\\rangle$ branch.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, inilalapat ang $B_{\\rm ref}$ sa $|0\\rangle$ branch lamang.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this point, the two branches have an extra relative phase. To remove it, we apply the ancilla phase gate\n"
msgstr "Sa puntong ito, may karagdagang relative phase ang dalawang branch. Upang alisin ito, inilalapat natin ang ancilla phase gate\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"P(-E_{\\rm vac}t)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"P(-E_{\\rm vac}t)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This transforms the state as\n"
msgstr "Binabago nito ang state bilang\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, up to an irrelevant global phase, we finally prepared\n"
msgstr "Kaya naman, maliban sa isang hindi mahalagang global phase, naihanda na natin sa huli ang\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the next code block, we implement this control-free circuit.\n"
msgstr "Sa susunod na code block, ipinapatupad natin ang control-free circuit na ito.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/790e5e0c-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/790e5e0c-1.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpilation {#transpilation}"
msgstr "Transpilation {#transpilation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, we transpile the controlled- and control-free circuits to become executable on the hardware.\n"
"Let's compare the result of the transpiled circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon, ini-transpile natin ang controlled- at control-free na circuits upang maging executable sa hardware.\n"
"Ihambing natin ang resulta ng mga na-transpile na circuits.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next step is to submit the same parameterized circuit for several values of $d$. For each $d$, we estimate four expectation values: $X\\otimes I$, $Y\\otimes I$, $X\\otimes (H-T)$, and $Y\\otimes (H-T)$. These four numbers are then combined into the complex first-row elements $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$ and $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}$.\n"
msgstr "Ang susunod na hakbang ay ang pagsumite ng parehong parameterized circuit para sa ilang halaga ng $d$. Para sa bawat $d$, tinatantiya natin ang apat na expectation value: $X\\otimes I$, $Y\\otimes I$, $X\\otimes (H-T)$, at $Y\\otimes (H-T)$. Ang apat na numerong ito ay pagkatapos pinagsasama upang bumuo ng complex first-row elements na $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$ at $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, $\\mathcal{S}_{00}=1$ and $\\mathcal{H}_{00}=\\langle\\psi_{0}|(H-T)|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\langle\\psi_{0}|H|\\psi_{0}\\rangle-\\tau$ can be classically calculated since $\\lvert\\psi_0\\rangle$ is sparse, so we skip the $d=0$ case.\n"
msgstr "Dito, $\\mathcal{S}_{00}=1$ at $\\mathcal{H}_{00}=\\langle\\psi_{0}|(H-T)|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\langle\\psi_{0}|H|\\psi_{0}\\rangle-\\tau$ ay maaaring kalkulahin nang classical dahil sparse ang $\\lvert\\psi_0\\rangle$, kaya't nilalaktawan natin ang kaso ng $d=0$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After estimating the projected matrices, we regularize and solve the GEVP\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c} = E\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"The smallest generalized eigenvalue gives the KQD estimate of the ground-state energy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos tantiyahin ang mga projected matrices, nire-regularize natin at nilulutas ang GEVP\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c} = E\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"Ang pinakamaliit na generalized eigenvalue ay nagbibigay ng KQD estimate ng ground-state energy.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we solve the generalized eigenvalue problem using the matrices reconstructed from the circuit estimates.\n"
"In an ideal statevector calculation with exact real-time evolution, this should reproduce the exact projected result.\n"
"In practice, deviations can come from Trotterization, sampling error, and numerical instability of the overlap matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon nilulutas natin ang generalized eigenvalue problem gamit ang mga matrices na muling ibinuo mula sa mga estimate ng circuit.\n"
"Sa isang ideal na statevector calculation na may eksaktong real-time evolution, dapat itong maireproduce ang eksaktong projected result.\n"
"Sa praktika, maaaring magmula ang mga deviation sa Trotterization, sampling error, at numerical instability ng overlap matrix.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We observe how the energy converges as we increase the dimension of the Krylov subspace.\n"
msgstr "Sinusuri natin kung paano nag-converge ang energy habang pinapataas natin ang dimension ng Krylov subspace.\n"

