# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The previous section used a 12-qubit model so that the statevector simulation could be used as a diagnostic. We now scale the same KQD workflow to a 30-qubit Heisenberg chain and prepare the workload for execution on IBM Quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "Gumamit ang nakaraang seksyon ng 12-qubit na modelo upang magamit ang statevector simulation bilang diagnostic. Ngayon ay pinapalaki natin ang parehong KQD workflow sa isang 30-qubit na Heisenberg chain at inihahanda ang workload para sa execution sa IBM Quantum hardware.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1-4 compressed into a single code block {#steps-1-4-compressed-into-a-single-code-block}"
msgstr "Steps 1-4 compressed into a single code block {#steps-1-4-compressed-into-a-single-code-block}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we now put all of these details together into a singular workflow at a larger scale, which is then run on our real quantum hardware. In this section, we apply realistic error-mitigation settings to improve the reliability of the results. Since the matrix elements corresponding to different values of $d$ can be evaluated in parallel, we use `Batch` mode to execute them efficiently.\n"
msgstr "Dito, pinagsasama-sama na natin ang lahat ng detalyeng ito sa iisang workflow sa mas malaking sukat, na pagkatapos ay pinapatakbo sa ating tunay na quantum hardware. Sa seksyong ito, inilalapat natin ang makatotohanang mga setting ng error mitigation upang pahusayin ang reliability ng mga resulta. Dahil ang mga matrix element na katumbas ng iba't ibang halaga ng $d$ ay maaaring suriin nang parallel, ginagamit natin ang `Batch` mode upang epektibong i-execute ang mga ito.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
